  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness, specifically identifying a lottery that is more right-skewed — meaning a greater portion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. In this case, Lottery B has only a 1% chance of 0€, which is unfavorable, while 99% is favorable. Thus, B is left-skewed, not right-skewed. Lottery A has no unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, neither lottery is right-skewed, so the decision reason does not apply. The individual's report does not mention skewness, right-skewness, or any comparison based on the distribution of unfavorable outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the perceived fairness of outcomes and downplays the 1% chance of 0€. There is no reference to the structure of the probability distribution in terms of skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reason is not applicable to the problem, and the report lacks any mention of it. Hence, the individual did not use the decision reason.",
